-- title:
--   Fixed places of a twisted q²-Frobenius on the Drinfeld curve
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2=\mathbb F_{q^2}$, such that the coordinate ring `CoordRing q k` of the Drinfeld curve (the quotient of $k[x,y]$ by the ideal generated by $xy^q-x^qy-1$) is a domain and its fraction field $F=$ `drinfeldFunctionField q k` satisfies `IsCurveOver k`, i.e. every nonzero element of $F$ has a degree-zero principal divisor, every place has residue field finite over $k$, and $\Omega_{F/k}$ is free of rank one. Let $\varphi\colon F\to F$ be a $k$-algebra endomorphism whose underlying ring map is integral and which sends the images $X,Y\in F$ of the coordinates $x,y$ to $X^{q^2}$, $Y^{q^2}$. Let $p$ lie in `hSubgroup q`, the kernel of the character $(g,\zeta)\mapsto \det(g)\,\zeta^{q+1}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Z/q)\times\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$; write $g$ for the matrix underlying the first component and $c\in k$ for the image of the second component under $\mathbb F_{q^2}\to k$. Then the number of places $w$ of $F$ over $k$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $k$, proper, and principal ideal rings) for which the place $\varphi^{-1}(\mathcal O_w)$ obtained by restriction along $\varphi$ equals the translate of $w$ by the automorphism `hFunctionFieldAction q k p` of $F$, equals the number of pairs $(a,b)\in k^2$ with $ab^q-a^qb=1$, $c\,(g_{00}a^{q^2}+g_{10}b^{q^2})=a$ and $c\,(g_{01}a^{q^2}+g_{11}b^{q^2})=b$ (entries of $g$ mapped into $k$ through $\mathbb Z/q\to\mathbb F_{q^2}\to k$), plus the number of $t\in\mathbb Z/q$ with $tg_{00}+g_{10}=t\,(tg_{01}+g_{11})$, plus $1$ if $g_{01}=0$ and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the fixed-point count for a twisted $q^2$-Frobenius on the Drinfeld curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$: the places fixed by $\varphi$ composed with the action of $p\in H$ split into affine points of the curve fixed by the twisted Frobenius and the places at infinity, which correspond to the points of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ fixed by $g$ in the row action. It is used by [`DrinfeldCurve.natCard_place_restrictAlong_eq_smul_of_torus`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.natCard_place_restrictAlong_eq_smul_of_torus), where the right-hand side is evaluated for $p$ in a torus.
